-- A '-' glued to digits lexes as one token wherever it appears; the grammar
-- reads it as a literal where an expression may start and as a subtraction
-- after an operand. So every spelling of a subtraction below agrees, spacing
-- and line breaks included, and none of them is an application.
-- @expect-type: (((Int * Int) * (Int * Int)) * ((Int * Double) * Int))!{}
-- @expect-value: Pure: (((-3, 9), (9, 9)), ((5, -0.25), -4))
do n <- return 10 in
return (((-3, n-1), ((n) - 1, 10-1)), ((3 - -2, -0.25),
1-2-3))
